- Exceptions
- Reporting cache where useful

# Products and fixed recipes

There are three candle products. Each is sold individually or as a fixed box.

1. Christmas Tree
   - Individual
   - Box of 7

2. Bulk Christmas Tree Small
   - Individual
   - Box of 3

3. Bulk Christmas Tree Tall
   - Individual
   - Box of 3

A customer cannot mix candle types inside these boxes. The compositions are fixed.

Model the initial recipes as:

A. CHRISTMAS_TREE_BOX_7
   - Sale variation: Christmas Tree / Box of 7
   - Consume 7 units of Christmas Tree / Individual
   - Consume 1 unit of the mapped seven-candle packaging box

B. BULK_CHRISTMAS_TREE_SMALL_BOX_3
   - Sale variation: Bulk Christmas Tree Small / Box of 3
   - Consume 3 units of Bulk Christmas Tree Small / Individual
   - Consume 1 unit of the mapped small three-candle packaging box

C. BULK_CHRISTMAS_TREE_TALL_BOX_3
   - Sale variation: Bulk Christmas Tree Tall / Box of 3
   - Consume 3 units of Bulk Christmas Tree Tall / Individual
   - Consume 1 unit of the mapped tall three-candle packaging box

The small and tall box recipes might use:

- Two different packaging variations, or
- The same shared three-candle packaging variation

The setup UI must support either arrangement. It must be legal for the two recipes to map to the same packaging variation.

Do not hard-code Square catalogue IDs. Build a first-run setup screen that retrieves the Square catalogue and lets the administrator map Square item variation IDs to these roles:

- CHRISTMAS_TREE_INDIVIDUAL
- CHRISTMAS_TREE_BOX_7
- BULK_CHRISTMAS_TREE_SMALL_INDIVIDUAL
- BULK_CHRISTMAS_TREE_SMALL_BOX_3
- BULK_CHRISTMAS_TREE_TALL_INDIVIDUAL
- BULK_CHRISTMAS_TREE_TALL_BOX_3
- BOX_7_PACKAGING
- BOX_3_SMALL_PACKAGING
- BOX_3_TALL_PACKAGING

Allow BOX_3_SMALL_PACKAGING and BOX_3_TALL_PACKAGING to point to the same Square variation.

Use Square catalogue object IDs for all matching. Never match production orders using item names, variation names, prices, SKUs, or fuzzy text.

Names can be displayed to users but IDs control the logic.

# Required Square catalogue arrangement

The application should validate and explain this arrangement:

- The three individual candle variations must be stock tracked in Square.
- The raw packaging variations must be stock tracked in Square.
- The three box-for-sale variations should not have independent stock tracking because they are assembled on demand.
- Individual candle sales are automatically reflected in Square inventory.
- The application must not deduct individual sales a second time.
- Box sales are expanded by the application into their candle and packaging components.
- The box-for-sale variation itself is not a physical stock item.

Recommended Square structure:

- Item: Christmas Tree
  - Variation: Individual
  - Variation: Box of 7

- Item: Bulk Christmas Tree Small
  - Variation: Individual
  - Variation: Box of 3

- Item: Bulk Christmas Tree Tall
  - Variation: Individual
  - Variation: Box of 3

- Raw-material variation: Empty Box for 7 Candles
- Raw-material variation: Empty Box for 3 Small Candles
- Raw-material variation: Empty Box for 3 Tall Candles

The last two can be replaced by one shared Empty Box for 3 Candles variation.

The application must not automatically modify the Square catalogue in the MVP. It should retrieve, map, validate, and display clear corrective instructions.

Treat any of the following as configuration warnings or blocking errors:

- A mapped catalogue ID no longer exists
- A component variation is not stock tracked
- A box sale variation is itself stock tracked
- A mapped object is not an ITEM_VARIATION
- Two unrelated roles accidentally reference the same variation
- A Square stock-conversion configuration would cause candle inventory to be deducted both by Square and this application

Do not implement Square Retail Plus stock conversion in the MVP. Detect a conflicting stock-conversion configuration where possible and block inventory writes until it is resolved.

# Core user workflow

At the market, my wife uses only Square POS.

Example sale:

- Christmas Tree / Box of 7
- Quantity 2
- Square records the actual sale price and payment

During the next sync, the application must infer:

- Christmas Tree individual stock: minus 14
- Seven-candle packaging stock: minus 2
- Box sales quantity: 2
- Box revenue: use the actual value recorded on the Square order

She must not select seven component candles.
She must not open this application during the sale.
She must not enter the same transaction later.
She must not maintain a second spreadsheet.

Another example:

- Christmas Tree / Individual quantity 1
- Christmas Tree / Box of 7 quantity 1

Expected inventory result:

- Square automatically deducts 1 Christmas Tree candle for the individual line.
- The application deducts 7 Christmas Tree candles for the box line.
- The application deducts 1 seven-candle packaging box.
- Overall physical Christmas Tree stock falls by 8.
- Revenue comes from the two actual Square line items.

